# Start Child Agents

This Livebook starts and stops one owned child Agent through Directives.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define The Child

```elixir
defmodule ChildGuide.Worker do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "child_guide_worker"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{jobs: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)})
  end
end
```

## Define The Parent

```elixir
defmodule ChildGuide.Parent do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "child_guide_parent"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{desired: Zoi.boolean() |> Zoi.default(false)})
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/children"

    route "child.start" do
      action _input, name: "child_guide_start", context: context do
        directive =
          Jido.Agent.Directive.spawn_agent(
            ChildGuide.Worker,
            :worker,
            opts: %{id: "child-worker"},
            restart: :transient
          )

        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | desired: true}, [directive]}
      end

      define :start_worker
    end

    route "child.stop" do
      action _input, name: "child_guide_stop", context: context do
        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | desired: false},
         [Jido.Agent.Directive.stop_child(:worker)]}
      end

      define :stop_worker
    end

    route "jido.agent.child.*" do
      action _input, name: "child_guide_lifecycle", context: context do
        {:ok, context.agent_state}
      end
    end
  end
end
```

The parent stores desired business state. The Agent Server stores the child PID
and monitor in runtime state.

## Start The Parent And Child

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, parent} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    ChildGuide.Parent,
    id: "child-parent"
  )

{:ok, committed} = ChildGuide.Parent.start_worker(parent)

child =
  Enum.reduce_while(1..100, nil, fn _, _ ->
    case Jido.AgentServer.children(parent)[:worker] do
      nil ->
        Process.sleep(10)
        {:cont, nil}

      value ->
        {:halt, value}
    end
  end)

{committed.state.desired, child.pid, child.id}
```

The parent commit can finish before child startup. The bounded loop waits for
post-commit Directive dispatch.

## Stop The Child

```elixir
{:ok, committed} = ChildGuide.Parent.stop_worker(parent)

true =
  Enum.reduce_while(1..100, false, fn _, _ ->
    if Jido.AgentServer.children(parent)[:worker] do
      Process.sleep(10)
      {:cont, false}
    else
      {:halt, true}
    end
  end)

committed.state.desired
```

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(parent)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Continue with [Ownership, Orphans, And Remote Children](ownership-orphans-and-remote-children.md).
